    "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate experienced a gross prior year reserve release of GBP 16.1 million in 2020, primarily driven by favorable claims development across various classes. Long-tail casualty classes contributed a GBP 5.4 million release, while Auto and other miscellaneous specialty classes, including a large Irish motor account from 2012-16, contributed a GBP 6.2 million gross back-year release due to better than expected performance. The remaining GBP 4.5 million release came from the short-tail account, likely including property lines. Favorable legal rulings for Superstorm Sandy (2012) and a successful arbitration for a Canadian wildfire reinsurance contract (2015) also contributed to the releases. However, there was a roughly 10% deterioration in gross Hurricane Irma (2017) losses.",
